=== 1. one task, collected later ===
  spawned, doing something else meanwhile...
  sum(1..1000) = 500500

=== 2. a producer and a consumer, joined by a channel ===
  received  alpha
  received  bravo
  received  charlie
  received  delta
  produced  4, received  4

=== 3. polling instead of waiting ===
  done before the gate opens?  false
  task returned  finished

=== 4. a failing task reports, it does not crash ===
  value=
  failure=ERROR:task failed: integer division by zero at examples/concurrency/worker_pool.mut:103:12 context=builtin.task_wait

=== 5. when the work IS an array, use pmap ===
  [1, 4, 9, 16, 25, 36, 49, 64]

=== 6. work the program never collects still finishes ===
  program body done; the runtime will wait for the detached task

  the detached task finished after the program body did
